source: crates/aidp-cli/tests/cli_surface.rs
expression: normalized
---
Run lifecycle: init, start, state, summary, reconcile, resume anchors

Usage: <BIN> run [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init           Create a run: allocate its id and directory, write its state and print the id
  start          `run init` + `workflow emit` in one call. Same flags as `init`, plus repeatable `--input k=v` (a repeated key accumulates into a JSON array)
  exec           Run a template natively: the daemon (or `--foreground`, in-process) drives every stage through agent sessions, with no Workflow tool involved
  state          Print a run's state (text by default; `--format json-compact` for JSON)
  summary        Print a human-readable summary of a run
  reconcile      Fold a Workflow result file (`--from`) back into run-state. Exits 0 even with scope_violations; exits 4 (policy refusal) on a vault leak
  plan-exec      Write the typed execution plan of a run to `execution-plan.json` and print its path
  record-resume  Persist resume state: Workflow runId, approved gates, `--pending-gate`, `--crossed-boundary`, or `--from-result`; explicit flags win over the file
  stage-tokens   Read a sub-agent's token usage from the Claude projects directory
  verify         Replay verify_outputs over a run's declared outputs: annotation only, exits 0. `--stage` restricts to one stage
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --no-knowledge
          Leave the compile-time `## Knowledge` block out of the stage prompts

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
